---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology"
  description="How feedme.design sources, tests and corrects its e-commerce UX research."
>
  <PageHead title="Methodology" blurb="The aim is for anyone to repeat what we did, or at least see exactly where our numbers came from." />
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 style="margin-top: 0">Breakdowns</h2>
    <p>
      A breakdown examines a real shopping flow step by step. We state the device, the browser, the country and the date of each walkthrough, and we keep dated screenshots so that a later redesign can't quietly rewrite what we saw. Where a conclusion is our own judgement rather than a measured result, the text says so.
    </p>

    <h2>Data studies</h2>
    <p>
      Every study publishes its sample size, how the sample was chosen, the collection window and the method used. Where the raw figures can be shared they're offered as a download. We report what the data showed even when it undercuts the neat story, and we flag any limits that affect how far the result should be generalised.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party sources</h2>
    <p>
      We link to the original publisher rather than a summary of it, and we record the date we last checked each source. Figures we haven't been able to trace back to a primary source are left out.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If we get something wrong we fix it in the article, add an updated date and describe the change at the foot of the piece, so the record stays honest.
    </p>

    <h2>Citing our work</h2>
    <p>
      Each article ends with a ready-made citation. You're welcome to quote our figures with a link back to the page they came from.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
